# Assignment 4.1 — Student Registration Form

## Question 1: Build the form inside a `<form>` tag.

**Answer:**

```html
<form>
    <!-- Form fields will be added here -->
</form>
```

**Explanation:** The `<form>` tag is used to create a form that collects information from users.

## Question 2: Add a proper `<label>` for each field.

**Answer:**

```html
<label for="fullName">Full Name:</label>
<input type="text" id="fullName" name="fullName">
```

**Explanation:** The `<label>` tag describes the purpose of an input field. Its `for` attribute should match the input's `id`.

## Question 3: Use the correct input types.

**Answer:**

```html
<input type="text" id="fullName" name="fullName">
<input type="email" id="email" name="email">
<input type="password" id="password" name="password">
<input type="tel" id="phone" name="phone">
<input type="number" id="age" name="age">
```

**Explanation:**

* `text` — Accepts text such as a person's name.
* `email` — Checks that the entered value has a valid email format.
* `password` — Hides the entered password characters.
* `tel` — Accepts a telephone number.
* `number` — Accepts numerical values such as age.

## Question 4: Give each input a unique `id` and meaningful `name`.

**Answer:**

```html
<input type="text" id="fullName" name="fullName">
<input type="email" id="email" name="email">
<input type="password" id="password" name="password">
```

**Explanation:** The `id` uniquely identifies an element on the page. The `name` identifies the field when form data is submitted.

## Question 5: Add `required` on mandatory fields.

**Answer:**

```html
<input type="text" id="fullName" name="fullName" required>
<input type="email" id="email" name="email" required>
<input type="password" id="password" name="password" required>
```

**Explanation:** The `required` attribute prevents the browser from submitting the form when a mandatory field is empty.

## Question 6: Complete the form with a submit button.

**Answer:**

```html
<button type="submit">Register</button>
```

**Explanation:** The submit button attempts to submit the form after the browser checks its built-in validation rules.

## Question 7: Create the complete Student Registration Form.

**Answer:**

Save this complete code as `registration.html`.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>Student Registration Form</title>
</head>

<body>

    <h1>Student Registration Form</h1>

    <p>Please fill in the details below to register.</p>

    <form action="#" method="post">

        <!-- Full Name -->
        <label for="fullName">Full Name:</label>
        <input
            type="text"
            id="fullName"
            name="fullName"
            placeholder="Enter your full name"
            autocomplete="name"
            required
        >

        <br><br>

        <!-- Email -->
        <label for="email">Email:</label>
        <input
            type="email"
            id="email"
            name="email"
            placeholder="Enter your email"
            autocomplete="email"
            required
        >

        <br><br>

        <!-- Password -->
        <label for="password">Password:</label>
        <input
            type="password"
            id="password"
            name="password"
            placeholder="Create a password"
            autocomplete="new-password"
            required
        >

        <br><br>

        <!-- Phone Number -->
        <label for="phone">Phone Number:</label>
        <input
            type="tel"
            id="phone"
            name="phone"
            placeholder="Enter your phone number"
            autocomplete="tel"
            required
        >

        <br><br>

        <!-- Age -->
        <label for="age">Age:</label>
        <input
            type="number"
            id="age"
            name="age"
            placeholder="Enter your age"
            min="1"
            max="120"
            required
        >

        <br><br>

        <!-- Submit Button -->
        <button type="submit">Register</button>

    </form>

</body>

</html>
```

## Submission Requirements

1. Save the file as `registration.html`.
2. Open the file in a browser.
3. Fill in the form fields and test the required-field validation.
4. Take a screenshot of the working form.
5. Submit `registration.html` and the screenshot.

**Note:** This is a front-end form. The `action="#"` attribute does not store registration details in a database. Saving student data requires a suitable server or form-handling service.
